# ==========================================
# HITL Experiment Scenario - Baseline & Conflicts
# Manual collision geometry (CRECONFS avoided - see notes below)
# ==========================================

# --- System & Camera Initialization ---
# Enable Conflict Detection (crucial for visual alerts on the radar)
00:00:00.00> CDMETHOD ON
# Start the FOV-filtered aircraft logger and the operator-command logger
# (see bluesky/plugins/hitl_fovaclog.py and bluesky/plugins/hitl_opcmdlog.py).
# These MUST be turned on here, inside the scenario, rather than typed
# manually beforehand in the console - loading a scenario always resets
# the sim first, which closes any logger that was already open and
# silently drops all further rows.
00:00:00.00> FOVACLOG ON
00:00:00.00> OPCMDLOG ON
# Start recording every subsequent stack command (incl. manual resolutions)
# to a fresh, timestamped, replayable scenario file. For per-command
# timestamps in CSV form (incl. sender id), see OPCMDLOG instead.
00:00:00.00> SAVEIC HITL_2con_run
# Center radar screen on a specific location (lat, lon)
00:00:00.00> PAN 52.0 4.5
# Set initial zoom level to fit the experiment area
00:00:00.00> ZOOM 0.8

# --- Background Traffic (Baseline) ---
# Injected immediately to create a realistic but manageable workload.
# These aircraft cruise at FL180-FL300, clear of the FL100/FL150 conflict
# geometry below, so they never trigger spurious alerts.
00:00:00.00> CRE BG1, B738, 52.8, 3.5, 090, FL200, 300
00:00:00.00> CRE BG2, A320, 51.2, 5.5, 270, FL220, 300
00:00:00.00> CRE BG3, B744, 52.5, 4.8, 180, FL300, 350
00:00:00.00> CRE BG4, MD11, 51.5, 3.8, 360, FL180, 280

# ==========================================
# Trial 1: Head-On Conflict (180 deg, dpsi) @ FL100
# ==========================================
# TARG1 flies due east (090) at 250 kt from t=00:00:05.
00:00:05.00> CRE TARG1, B738, 52.0000, 3.5000, 090, FL100, 250

# INTRUDER1 is placed manually so that, flying due west (270) at 250 kt,
# it meets TARG1 head-on exactly 60s later (both arrive at ~52.0000N 3.6598E
# at simulation t=00:01:30). Geometry (great-circle, small-angle approx at
# 52N): TARG1 covers 250kt*85s = 5.90 NM east of its t=5s spawn point by
# t=90s; INTRUDER1 is spawned 250kt*60s = 4.17 NM further east of that
# meeting point so it closes the gap in exactly 60s.
00:00:30.00> CRE INTRUDER1, B738, 52.0000, 3.7725, 270, FL100, 250

# ==========================================
# Trial 2: Crossing Conflict (90 deg, dpsi) @ FL150
# ==========================================
# TARG2 flies due north (360) at 250 kt, INTRUDER2 flies due east (090) at
# 250 kt. Both spawned at t=00:02:00 and both placed 250kt*90s = 6.25 NM
# from the shared meeting point (51.6042N 5.0000E), so they cross paths
# at a right angle exactly 90s later, at t=00:03:30, same altitude (FL150).
00:02:00.00> CRE TARG2, A320, 51.5000, 5.0000, 360, FL150, 250
00:02:00.00> CRE INTRUDER2, A320, 51.6042, 4.8323, 090, FL150, 250
